msgid "Tipo de retorno"
msgstr "Tipo de retorno"

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.fir_channel:3 of
msgid ""
"The channel is built with :func:`scipy.signal.firwin` using "
"``pass_zero=True`` (true low-pass) and unit sampling frequency "
"normalisation (``fs=2.0``). The DC gain of the resulting filter is "
"normalised to ``1.0``."
msgstr ""
"The channel is built with :func:`scipy.signal.firwin` using "
"``pass_zero=True`` (true low-pass) and unit sampling frequency "
"normalisation (``fs=2.0``). The DC gain of the resulting filter is "
"normalised to ``1.0``."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.fir_channel:9 of
msgid ""
"Normalised cutoff frequency ``ω_c / π ∈ (0, 1)``. Defaults to ``0.99`` — "
"i.e. the channel passes almost everything, mimicking a very lightly band-"
"limited link."
msgstr ""
"Normalised cutoff frequency ``ω_c / π ∈ (0, 1)``. Defaults to ``0.99`` — "
"i.e. the channel passes almost everything, mimicking a very lightly band-"
"limited link."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.fir_channel:12 of
msgid "Length of the FIR filter in samples. Must be a positive integer."
msgstr "Length of the FIR filter in samples. Must be a positive integer."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.fir_channel:13 of
msgid ""
"Window function passed through to ``firwin``. Any name accepted by "
":func:`scipy.signal.get_window` is valid — common choices are "
"``\"hamming\"``, ``\"hann\"``, ``\"blackman\"``."
msgstr ""
"Window function passed through to ``firwin``. Any name accepted by "
":func:`scipy.signal.get_window` is valid — common choices are "
"``\"hamming\"``, ``\"hann\"``, ``\"blackman\"``."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.fir_channel:17 of
msgid ""
"* **r** (*ndarray, shape (N,)*) -- Received signal, ``s`` filtered "
"through the FIR coefficients. * **h** (*ndarray, shape (num_taps,)*) -- "
"Filter coefficients, useful for overlaying the channel response   on PSD "
"plots."
msgstr ""
"* **r** (*ndarray, shape (N,)*) -- Received signal, ``s`` filtered "
"through the FIR coefficients. * **h** (*ndarray, shape (num_taps,)*) -- "
"Filter coefficients, useful for overlaying the channel response   on PSD "
"plots."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.fir_channel:17 of
msgid ""
"**r** (*ndarray, shape (N,)*) -- Received signal, ``s`` filtered through "
"the FIR coefficients."
msgstr ""
"**r** (*ndarray, shape (N,)*) -- Received signal, ``s`` filtered through "
"the FIR coefficients."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.fir_channel:18 of
msgid ""
"**h** (*ndarray, shape (num_taps,)*) -- Filter coefficients, useful for "
"overlaying the channel response on PSD plots."
msgstr ""
"**h** (*ndarray, shape (num_taps,)*) -- Filter coefficients, useful for "
"overlaying the channel response on PSD plots."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.fir_channel:22 of
msgid "Notas"
msgstr "Notas"

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.fir_channel:23 of
msgid ""
"Unlike :func:`ideal_channel`, this function returns the filter taps "
"alongside the filtered signal.  It therefore does **not** satisfy "
":class:`~chaotic_pfc.comms.protocols.Channel` (which expects a single "
"``NDArray`` return)."
msgstr ""
"Unlike :func:`ideal_channel`, this function returns the filter taps "
"alongside the filtered signal.  It therefore does **not** satisfy "
":class:`~chaotic_pfc.comms.protocols.Channel` (which expects a single "
"``NDArray`` return)."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.awgn:3 of
msgid ""
"The noise power is ``E[|sig|²] / 10^(SNR/10)``, so a higher SNR means "
"less noise."
msgstr ""
"The noise power is ``E[|sig|²] / 10^(SNR/10)``, so a higher SNR means "
"less noise."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.awgn:6
#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_impulsive:7
#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_multipath:7 of
msgid "Signal samples, shape ``(N,)``."
msgstr "Signal samples, shape ``(N,)``."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.awgn:7 of
msgid ""
"Signal-to-noise ratio in dB.  ``snr_db → ∞`` gives the original signal; "
"``snr_db = 0`` gives equal-power noise."
msgstr ""
"Signal-to-noise ratio in dB.  ``snr_db → ∞`` gives the original signal; "
"``snr_db = 0`` gives equal-power noise."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.awgn:9 of
msgid ""
"NumPy ``Generator``.  ``None`` (default) creates a fresh "
"``default_rng()`` with no fixed seed, so results are not reproducible "
"across calls.  Pass a seeded generator for deterministic noise."
msgstr ""
"NumPy ``Generator``.  ``None`` (default) creates a fresh "
"``default_rng()`` with no fixed seed, so results are not reproducible "
"across calls.  Pass a seeded generator for deterministic noise."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.awgn:14 of
msgid "Signal with additive white Gaussian noise."
msgstr "Signal with additive white Gaussian noise."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.awgn:18 of
msgid "Referências"
msgstr "Referências"

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.awgn:19 of
msgid "Haykin. \"Communication Systems.\" 4th ed., Wiley, 2001."
msgstr "Haykin. \"Communication Systems.\" 4th ed., Wiley, 2001."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_impulsive:3 of
msgid ""
"A fraction *prob_impulse* of samples receive an additional impulse of "
"randomised sign and amplitude *amp_factor* × ``std(sig)`` on top of the "
"AWGN background."
msgstr ""
"A fraction *prob_impulse* of samples receive an additional impulse of "
"randomised sign and amplitude *amp_factor* × ``std(sig)`` on top of the "
"AWGN background."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_impulsive:8 of
msgid "Background AWGN signal-to-noise ratio in dB."
msgstr "Background AWGN signal-to-noise ratio in dB."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_impulsive:9 of
msgid "Probability a sample is hit by an impulse (e.g. 0.01 = 1 %)."
msgstr "Probability a sample is hit by an impulse (e.g. 0.01 = 1 %)."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_impulsive:10 of
msgid "Impulse amplitude in multiples of the signal std."
msgstr "Impulse amplitude in multiples of the signal std."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_impulsive:11
#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_multipath:11 of
msgid "Random generator.  ``None`` creates a fresh ``default_rng()``."
msgstr "Random generator.  ``None`` creates a fresh ``default_rng()``."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_impulsive:13 of
msgid "Signal with AWGN + Middleton Class-A impulsive noise."
msgstr "Signal with AWGN + Middleton Class-A impulsive noise."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_multipath:3 of
msgid ""
"Simulates a frequency-selective channel by summing delayed copies of the "
"input.  Output power is normalised to the input power, then AWGN is added"
" at the requested SNR."
msgstr ""
"Simulates a frequency-selective channel by summing delayed copies of the "
"input.  Output power is normalised to the input power, then AWGN is added"
" at the requested SNR."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_multipath:8 of
msgid "AWGN signal-to-noise ratio after multipath combining, in dB."
msgstr "AWGN signal-to-noise ratio after multipath combining, in dB."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_multipath:9 of
msgid "Delay of each path in samples (default: ``[0, 3, 7, 15]``)."
msgstr "Delay of each path in samples (default: ``[0, 3, 7, 15]``)."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_multipath:10 of
msgid "Attenuation per path (default: ``[1.0, 0.6, 0.4, 0.2]``)."
msgstr "Attenuation per path (default: ``[1.0, 0.6, 0.4, 0.2]``)."

#: chaotic_pfc.comms.channel.channel_multipath:13 of
msgid "Multipath-combined signal with AWGN."
msgstr "Multipath-combined signal with AWGN."

